#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:2
msgid "How to use private Git submodules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:6
msgid "This guide is for :doc:`/commercial/index`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:8
msgid ""
"If you are using private Git repositories and they also contain private "
"Git submodules, you need to follow a few special steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:11
msgid ""
"When a project is created, a SSH key is automatically generated. You can "
"use this SSH key to give Read the Docs access to clone your private "
"submodules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:16
msgid ""
"You can manage which submodules Read the Docs should clone using a "
"configuration file. See :ref:`config-file/v2:submodules`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:19
msgid ""
"Make sure you are using ``SSH`` URLs for your submodules "
"(``git@github.com:readthedocs/readthedocs.org.git`` for example) in your "
"``.gitmodules`` file, not ``http`` URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:26
msgid "Table of contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:29
msgid "GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:31
msgid ""
"Since GitHub doesn't allow you to reuse a deploy key across different "
"repositories, you'll need to use `machine users "
"<https://developer.github.com/v3/guides/managing-deploy-keys/#machine-"
"users>`__ to give read access to several repositories using only one SSH "
"key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:35
msgid "Remove the SSH deploy key that was added to the main repository on GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:39
msgid ""
"If you are using our :ref:`reference/git-integration:GitHub App` to "
"connect your repository to Read the Docs, you can skip this step, because"
" access to your repository is controlled through the App instead of a "
"deploy key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:42
msgid ""
"Go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Deploy keys` of your repository on "
"GitHub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:43
msgid "Delete the key added by ``Read the Docs Commercial (readthedocs.com)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:45
msgid ""
"Create a GitHub user and give it read only permissions to all the "
"necessary repositories. You can do this by adding the account as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:48
msgid ""
"A `collaborator <https://help.github.com/en/github/setting-up-and-"
"managing-your-github-user-account/inviting-collaborators-to-a-personal-"
"repository>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:49
msgid ""
"An `outside collaborator <https://help.github.com/en/github/setting-up-"
"and-managing-organizations-and-teams/adding-outside-collaborators-to-"
"repositories-in-your-organization>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:50
msgid ""
"A `team in an organization <https://help.github.com/en/github/setting-up-"
"and-managing-organizations-and-teams/adding-organization-members-"
"to-a-team>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:52
msgid ""
"Attach the public SSH key from your project on Read the Docs to the "
"GitHub user you just created"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:54
msgid "Go to the user's settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:55
msgid "Click on :guilabel:`SSH and GPG keys`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:56
msgid "Click on :guilabel:`New SSH key`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:57
msgid ""
"Put a descriptive title and paste the :ref:`public SSH key from your Read"
" the Docs project <guides/creating-project-private-repository:Configuring"
" your repository>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:59
msgid "Click on :guilabel:`Add SSH key`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:62
msgid "Azure DevOps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:64
msgid ""
"Azure DevOps does not have per-repository SSH keys, but keys can be added"
" to a user instead. As long as this user has access to your main "
"repository and all its submodules, Read the Docs can clone all the "
"repositories with the same key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:70
msgid ""
":ref:`Allow access to your Azure DevOps repository with an SSH key "
"<guides/creating-project-private-repository:Configuring your "
"repository>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:73
msgid "Others"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/private-submodules.rst:75
msgid ""
"GitLab and Bitbucket allow you to reuse the same SSH key across different"
" repositories. Since Read the Docs already added the public SSH key on "
"your main repository, you only need to add it to each submodule "
"repository."
msgstr ""

